[section:semaphores Semaphores]

A semaphore is a synchronization primitive that limits concurrent access to a
shared resource through a counter of available permits. It does not necessarily
make access mutually exclusive: with `n` permits, up to `n` fibers may hold a
permit at the same time. Only a semaphore holding a single permit behaves like a
mutex (see [link mutex_types Mutex Types]), and even then, unlike a mutex, it
has no owner: a permit can be released by a different fiber (or thread) than the
one that acquired it.

A fiber calls [member_link semaphore..acquire] to take one permit, suspending
while none is available. [member_link semaphore..release] adds permits and
resumes waiting fibers.

[note Waiting fibers are woken by [member_link semaphore..release]; the order in
which they acquire permits is not specified.]

[class_heading semaphore]

        #include <boost/fiber/semaphore.hpp>

        namespace boost {
        namespace fibers {

        class semaphore {
        public:
            static constexpr std::size_t max() noexcept;

            explicit semaphore( std::size_t initial = 0);

            semaphore( semaphore const&) = delete;
            semaphore & operator=( semaphore const&) = delete;
            semaphore( semaphore &&) = delete;
            semaphore & operator=( semaphore &&) = delete;
            ~semaphore() = default;

            void release( std::size_t n = 1);

            void acquire();

            bool try_acquire();

            template< typename Clock, typename Duration >
            bool try_acquire_until( std::chrono::time_point< Clock, Duration > const& timeout_time);

            template< typename Rep, typename Period >
            bool try_acquire_for( std::chrono::duration< Rep, Period > const& timeout_duration);
        };

        }}

Instances of __semaphore__ are not copyable or movable.

[member_heading semaphore..max]

        static constexpr std::size_t max() noexcept;

[variablelist
[[Returns:] [The maximum number of permits the semaphore can hold.]]
]

[heading Constructor]

        explicit semaphore( std::size_t initial = 0);

[variablelist
[[Effects:] [Constructs a semaphore holding `initial` permits.]]
]

[heading Destructor]

        ~semaphore() = default;

[variablelist
[[Precondition:] [No fiber is blocked on `*this`.]]
]

[member_heading semaphore..release]

        void release( std::size_t n = 1);

[variablelist
[[Effects:] [Adds `n` permits and unblocks waiting fibers. Does nothing if `n`
is zero.]]
[[Requires:] [`n` does not exceed `max()` minus the current number of permits.]]
]

[member_heading semaphore..acquire]

        void acquire();

[variablelist
[[Effects:] [Blocks the calling fiber until a permit is available, then takes
one permit.]]
]

[member_heading semaphore..try_acquire]

        bool try_acquire();

[variablelist
[[Effects:] [Takes one permit if one is available, without blocking.]]
[[Returns:] [`true` if a permit was taken, `false` otherwise.]]
]

[template_member_heading semaphore..try_acquire_until]

        template< typename Clock, typename Duration >
        bool try_acquire_until( std::chrono::time_point< Clock, Duration > const& timeout_time);

[variablelist
[[Effects:] [Blocks the calling fiber until a permit is available or the
time point `timeout_time` is reached. If a permit becomes available, takes one.]]
[[Returns:] [`true` if a permit was taken, `false` on timeout.]]
]

[template_member_heading semaphore..try_acquire_for]

        template< typename Rep, typename Period >
        bool try_acquire_for( std::chrono::duration< Rep, Period > const& timeout_duration);

[variablelist
[[Effects:] [Equivalent to `try_acquire_until( std::chrono::steady_clock::now() + timeout_duration)`.]]
[[Returns:] [`true` if a permit was taken, `false` on timeout.]]
]

[endsect]
